⍝ 05 · Strings: reverse, case, split, palindromes, a Caesar cipher
⍝ Run:  dyalog sample-scripts/05-strings.apls

s←'APL is a language for thinking about arrays'
⎕←'reversed: ',⌽s
⎕←'upper:    ',1 ⎕C s
words←(' '≠s)⊆s
⎕←'words: ',⍕≢words
⎕←'longest: ',⊃words[⍒≢¨words]
⎕←'each word reversed: ',1↓∊' ',¨⌽¨words
⎕←'vowels: ',⍕+/s∊'aeiouAEIOU'

IsPal←{w←⎕C ⍵∩⎕A,⎕C ⎕A ⋄ w≡⌽w}
⎕←'palindromes:'
⎕←↑{⍵,' → ',(1+IsPal ⍵)⊃'no' 'yes'}¨'racecar' 'A man, a plan, a canal: Panama' 'apl'

⍝ Caesar cipher: shift each letter ⍺ places; other characters stay.
Caesar←{a←⎕C ⎕A ⋄ i←a⍳⍵ ⋄ m←i≤26 ⋄ r←⍵ ⋄ r[⍸m]←a[1+26|⍺+¯1+m/i] ⋄ r}
secret←3 Caesar 'attack at dawn'
⎕←'encrypted: ',secret
⎕←'decrypted: ',¯3 Caesar secret
